      dialogue: null,
      notes: 'Productive rule for regular past-tense verbs: /ɪd/ after base-final /t d/; /t/ after voiceless consonants except /t/; /d/ after vowels and voiced consonants except /d/. Voiceless set /p k f s ʃ tʃ θ/. Avoid adjective exceptions such as learned /ˈlɜrnɪd/. Place fingers on throat for voiced/voiceless contrast /s z/, /f v/. No extra vowel in booked/called. Asked can reduce in natural speech, but model clear /æskt/ for initial retrieval.',
