      title: 'BE GOING TO → BE GONNA + V', instruction: 'GONNA là cách ghi lại lời nói thân mật. Giữ AM / IS / ARE; động từ sau ở dạng gốc.',
      lines: ['ĐỌC RÕ', 'going to /ˈɡoʊɪŋ tə/', 'I’m going to CALL her.', 'She’s going to BOOK it.', 'We’re going to LEAVE soon.', 'Are you going to JOIN us?', 'NÓI THÂN MẬT', 'gonna [ˈɡənə]', 'I’m gonna CALL her.', 'She’s gonna BOOK it.', 'We’re gonna LEAVE soon.', 'Are you gonna JOIN us?', 'ĐI ĐẾN MỘT NƠI: GIỮ GOING TO', 'I’m going to work. = Tôi đang đi đến nơi làm việc.', 'I’m gonna work. = Tôi sẽ / định làm việc.'],
      dialogue: null,
      notes: 'IPA is a teaching model of a connected chunk; exact reduction varies. Do not insist every speaker drops /h/ in her/him or flaps /t/. In ask again, connect the final consonant to the next vowel. Capitalized words indicate one possible focus. Repeat with a different time, person or action. Keep the earlier L09 meaning distinction: I’ll answer it as an immediate decision versus I’m gonna call her tonight as an existing intention; neither pronunciation alone decides the meaning.',
