      title: 'Nói về sở thích, lựa chọn và trải nghiệm', instruction: 'Mỗi câu trả lời: ý chính + lý do hoặc ví dụ thật.',
      lines: ['What are you interested in at the moment?', 'Một sở thích hoặc điều muốn tìm hiểu.', 'What are you excited about?', 'Điều bạn mong đợi; có thể dùng EXCITED ABOUT.', 'Were you happy with your last purchase?', 'Một món đồ và điều bạn thích / chưa thích.', 'Who do you usually ask for advice?', 'Một người và lý do tin tưởng.', 'What are you going to try this weekend?', 'Một dự định, địa điểm hoặc người đi cùng.', 'Hỏi thêm theo câu trả lời, không chỉ chuyển sang câu tiếp theo.'],
      dialogue: null,
      notes: 'MINH: Are you interested in visiting the new adventure park on Sunday? I’m looking at the tickets now, and the view looks amazing. SARA: I’m excited about going somewhere new, but I’m afraid of heights. Is there anything to do on the ground? MINH: Are you serious? I saw a climbing photo on your phone yesterday. I thought you enjoyed it. SARA: That was my cousin in the photo. She’s good at climbing. I just took the pictures and waited for her! MINH: Okay, how about the street festival instead? There are local bands and an art market, so we can choose what we like. SARA: That sounds better. I talked to a friend about it yesterday, and she really enjoyed the music. MINH: Are you worried about the weather? Most of the festival is outdoors, and the tickets aren’t refundable. SARA: A little. I’m going to check the forecast before we buy anything. Does it make sense to wait until tomorrow? MINH: Yes, I agree with you. The price depends on the ticket type, but we can pay at the gate. There’s no need to decide now. SARA: Great. I’m going to ask my cousin to join us. Let’s talk about the plan tomorrow so we’re ready for Sunday. Support: adventure park=khu vui chơi mạo hiểm; heights=độ cao; refundable=có thể hoàn tiền; forecast=dự báo thời tiết. Are you serious? is friendly surprise, not criticism.',
      images: [],
