      dialogue: null,
      notes: 'RECEPTION: Hello. Are you here for the photography group? We’re waiting for a few more people before we start. VISITOR: Yes. I’m interested in taking photos around the city. I looked for this entrance yesterday, but the building was closed. RECEPTION: We usually open at ten on Sundays. You’re in the right place now. The group is meeting in Room Two. VISITOR: Can you explain this map to me? It looks different from the one on your website, so I’m not sure where to go. RECEPTION: Of course. Go past this desk, turn left and take the stairs. Room Two is upstairs, next to the lift. VISITOR: Thanks. Does it make sense to start with the beginner group? I’m good at outdoor photos, but I need help with portraits. RECEPTION: Yes. We’re going to start with a short practice session, then talk about the pictures together. You can ask the teacher for help. VISITOR: Great. Are those bags part of the session? Who do they belong to? I don’t want to leave my things in the wrong place. RECEPTION: They belong to the volunteers. Your group can use the shelves upstairs. There’s no need to pay for a locker. VISITOR: That’s helpful, thank you. I’m going to try today’s session first, then think about joining the full course. Support: portraits=ảnh chân dung; volunteers=tình nguyện viên; lift=thang máy; locker=tủ khóa.',
